CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "cff11fda-5f0d-450b-8113-6277664fb8e5",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T19:39:48Z",
  "ticket_id": "677d-a6a0-0c2e-4b9e",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "When CI llm-review produces a finding that violates the schema, the validation step detects it and triggers exactly one correction dispatch before findings are written to disk; if review.schema_correction_max_attempts=0 the correction step is skipped and the path goes directly to the synthetic-error path.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior and error-handling logic that persists after implementation, not a one-time migration or completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When correction dispatch returns schema-valid findings with the same number of findings as the input AND byte-for-byte preservation of frozen fields (severity, category, description, file_path, line_range, finding_id), CI llm-review proceeds with the corrected findings and the job passes. If correction returns valid JSON but a different finding count or mutates any frozen field, correction is treated as failed and the synthetic-error path fires.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior and validation rules that persist after implementation, defining how the correction dispatch mechanism operates ongoing"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When correction dispatch fails to produce valid findings (validation still fails, count drift, frozen-field mutation, exhausted retries, or max_attempts=0), a synthetic schema_error finding (severity: critical, type: \"parse_error\" \u2014 already recognized by validate-review-output.sh as exempt from cited_excerpt/reachability checks) is appended, the existing severity gate fires, and CI exits non-zero with a stderr diagnostic naming the specific schema errors. Verified by appending the synthetic and re-running validation \u2014 no infinite loop.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior for error handling and validation when correction dispatch fails, phrased as ongoing mechanism"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The validation step shells out to validate-review-output.sh code-review-dispatch <tmpfile> with an explicit subprocess timeout (default 60s). When the validator binary is missing/non-executable, the subprocess times out, or returns an unrecognized exit code, runner.py emits a critical stderr diagnostic and exits non-zero \u2014 never silently skipped. Local /dso:review and CI enforce identical rules (zero drift).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior where validation enforces explicit timeout handling and error reporting with consistency between local and CI environments"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A new config key review.schema_correction_max_attempts (default: 1, documented intended range: 0\u20133, hard ceiling: 3 to prevent runaway LLM cost) is added to CONFIGURATION-REFERENCE.md and dso-config.conf; the runner clamps any value above the ceiling to the ceiling and logs a warning.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capability where a configuration parameter exists with defined behavior (clamping and logging) that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Regression tests in tests/skills/dso_ci_review/test_runner_smoke.py cover: (a) valid findings pass through unchanged; (b) missing cited_excerpt \u2192 corrected \u2192 pass; (c) missing reachability on critical severity \u2192 corrected \u2192 pass; (d) repeated correction failure \u2192 synthetic schema_error \u2192 non-zero exit; (e) silent severity mutation during correction \u2192 treated as failure \u2192 synthetic schema_error. At least one test invokes validate-review-output.sh live (not mocked) to exercise the actual shell contract.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable test coverage and system behavior verification that persists after implementation, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Validation signal: run the updated CI llm-review path against the PR-80 diff (the diff that produced 8/11 invalid findings in bug d42d-8126). Verified outcome: zero synthetic schema_error findings appended (the reviewer's output passes schema validation on the first attempt or after one successful correction), and 100% of real findings contain non-empty cited_excerpt and the required reachability sentence (when severity is critical, important, or fragile). Document the schema-compliance rate in the PR description as evidence that the calibration problem is closed.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time validation task with a specific test case and completion criteria (documenting results as evidence of closure)"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
